# Git workflow

- Integration branch: `prototype`. Default branch `main` stays protected and is merged only when the whole project works.
- Kidus and teammates: branch off `prototype` (`ui/`, `feat/`, `api/`, `models/`, `fix/`), open a PR **into `prototype`**. Do not target `main` for day-to-day work.
- `prototype` is easy to merge (PR required, 0 approving reviews). `main` still needs PR + 1 approval.
- Never make `prototype` the GitHub default branch.

# No Cursor attribution

Never add Cursor as an author, committer, co-author, or contributor. Do not put `Co-authored-by: Cursor`, `Made-with: Cursor`, or the name Cursor in commit messages, README, or any tracked file. GitHub history must show only the human teammates. If a commit would get a Cursor trailer, recreate it without that trailer before pushing.
